  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: BFF authorization filters and handlers, the caller-scoped access seams (CallerRecordAccessProbe, IDataverseUserClient, the impersonated read seam), chat-session ownership (#863), and SPE container resolution. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal API endpoint filters (ADR-008) and ProblemDetails (ADR-019). Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task, for EACH of the 17 routes in the evidence file:
(1) the authorization subject is the exact id the handler consumes, taken from the same source the handler binds (route, body or query), and the decision is the caller's own Dataverse or SPE answer, or the caller's own session ownership;
(2) the decision runs before any app-only read or write;
(3) an unknown target and a forbidden target get identical responses (status, title, detail, reasonCode and extension keys; only correlation/trace ids may differ), and neither reaches the downstream service;
(4) no route acts on a client-supplied secondary id (a container, a tenant, an SPE pointer, a parent lookup) that was not authorized: the server derives it from the authorized record, refuses it, or ignores it;
(5) two dead routes are DELETED, POST /api/compose/documents/{documentSpeId}/promote and POST /api/v1/work-assignments, together with their tests and census entries (GET /api/v1/documents?containerId= is gated, not deleted);
(6) once task 167's guard governs each file, every surviving route passes it with no Pending waiver, and every Pending waiver task 167 added for these routes is deleted in this task's diff.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Every anchor below was read against the working tree on 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-03 (branch work/unified-access-control-r2 at b18a7d321; the files in scope are identical on task/uac-r2-157-b2-r2). Line numbers drift, so Step 0 re-verifies them. The BFF has no DefaultPolicy or FallbackPolicy, so a bare `.RequireAuthorization()` means "authenticated" and nothing more.

FINDING NUMBERS. F0-F16 are the array indexes in idor-group-166.json. Sweep row numbers: F0=#36, F1=#76, F2=#63, F3=#64, F4=#65, F5=#66, F6=#80, F7=#42, F8=#39, F9=#43, F10=#68, F11=#67, F12=#69, F13=#82, F14=#71, F15=#70, F16=#81.

EVIDENCE FILE. The verified findings were written to the session scratchpad: C:/Users/RALPHS~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--code-files-spaarke-wt-unified-access-control-r2/993ea642-9455-4e0e-8f57-ed99084c5e37/scratchpad/idor-group-166.json. The main session copies it to projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/evidence/idor-group-166.json before dispatch. Read the project copy first. If neither copy exists, use the sweep note rows above and this background; do not stop for it.

══ MEMORY (3 findings) ══
F7 GET /api/memory/records/{entityLogicalName}/{id:guid}. Route at `Api/Memory/MemoryGovernanceEndpoints.cs:122`; group `:79-82` carries RequireAuthorization and a rate limit only; handler `ReadRecordMemoryAsync` `:328-367`. The only check is `IMemoryAccessAuthorizer.CanCallerReadRecordAsync` (`:349`), implemented by `Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryAccessAuthorizer.cs:39-65`. It calls `IDataversePrivilegeChecker.HasReadPrivilegeAsync(oid, entity)` and IGNORES recordId (`:55-58`: "row-level OBO implementation (deferred)"). That is a TABLE privilege: any user with any-depth Read on sprk_matter reads any matter's record memory, secure matters included. `IMemoryItemStore.GetForRecordAsync` is app-only Cosmos. No client calls this route (grep of src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js} for "memory/records": 0 hits). Record-memory subject types written today: `MemoryWriteHandler.DefaultRecordSubjectType = "matter"` (`Services/Ai/Handlers/MemoryWriteHandler.cs:84`, an alias EntityAccessFilter maps to sprk_matters) and `"sprk_document"` (`Services/Compose/ComposeMemoryCapturer.cs:103`, NOT in EntityAccessFilter's map). Related but not the same defect: GitHub #616 (memory trust level and poisoning, a deferred security project).
F9 POST /api/memory/pins and F10 PUT /api/memory/pins/{pinId}. Routes at `Api/Memory/PinnedMemoryEndpoints.cs:158` and `:170`; group `:139-142`. `CreatePinAsync` (`:267`) and `UpdatePinAsync` (`:356`) store `request.MatterId` as sent (create: the `MatterId = …` initializer in the `new PinnedContextItem` block, ~`:298`; update: ~`:421`) with no check on the matter. `TryValidateCreateRequest` (~`:600-655`) requires matterId only for pinType matter-fact, BUT both handlers persist MatterId for EVERY pinType when it is non-blank. The read side is cross-user: `PinnedContextRepository.GetByMatterAsync` (`Services/Ai/Memory/PinnedContextRepository.cs:142-168`) filters on documentType and matterId only (no userId, no pinType). `ContextBinder.ResolvePinnedContextFragmentAsync` (`Services/Ai/Context/ContextBinder.cs:864-872`) injects the result into the prompt of EVERY user who chats on that matter, under "Treat them as authoritative context" (`:917`). A pin is therefore a write into a matter-scoped shared surface. The PUT ownership check (`existing.UserId == oid`) protects the pin, not the matter. The only other pin writer, the chat tool `ManagePinnedContextHandler` (`Services/Ai/Handlers/ManagePinnedContextHandler.cs:478`), always writes MatterId = null, so it is not a second door. Live clients: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/components/memory/PinnedMemoryEditDialog.tsx` (matterId is a free-text field), `src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/context/PinnedMemoryListWidget.tsx`, and `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/HardSlashExecutor.ts:492` (`/save-to-matter [id]`, pinType matter-fact).

══ COMPOSE (4 findings). The files belong to spaarkeai-compose-r8 (CLOSED, wrap-up PR open); coordinate through /conflict-check ══
F2 POST /api/compose/documents/{documentSpeId}/promote. Route at `Api/ComposeDocumentEndpoints.cs:36`; handler `Promote` `:245-295`; DTOs `PromoteComposeDocumentBody` (~`:414`) and `PromoteComposeDocumentResponse` (~`:420`), used only by this route. Group guard only (`Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs:30-32`). It takes tenantId from the BODY (`:258`, `:270`), never resolves the caller, and makes no OBO call on documentSpeId. `ComposeRecordResolution.RebindSessionDocumentIdAsync` rebinds ANY (body tenant, body session) with no owner check. It also creates root-owned sprk_document rows app-only for any SPE item id. NO CLIENT: the only "/promote" calls in src are `/api/ai/analysis/promote` (`HistoryOverlay.tsx:854`, `useReviewedDocumentAnalysis.ts:37`). The service method `IComposeService.PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` IS used internally by create-on-save and stays. The route is pinned in `tests/integration/contract/Api/Compose/ComposeRouteSurfaceContractTests.cs:65` and exercised by `ComposeEndpointsContractTests.cs` (`PostPromoteDocument_*` at ~`:265` and ~`:364`). The promote body carries no driveId, so the item cannot be checked as the caller without a contract change. Deletion is the fix.
F3 POST /api/compose/upload. Route at `Api/ComposeMountEndpoints.cs:30`; handler `Upload` `:89-223`; `ResolveRetainedBinaryAsync` `:365-389`. The tenant comes from the claim (correct), but body sessionId and documentId read the retained "doc-upload-binary" bytes from `ITenantCache` with no session-owner check. The handler returns the bytes, filename and projection, and `IComposeService.ProjectForMount(binary, fileName, ct, body.SessionId)` records a PDF-source marker on the named session. The same cache entries are written and read elsewhere only behind `.AddSessionOwnershipFilter()` (`Api/Ai/ChatDocumentEndpoints.cs`). The file is not in `SessionOwnershipGuardTests.BodyScopedSessionRoutes` (`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SessionOwnershipGuardTests.cs:~34-63`). Live client: `ComposeWorkspace.tsx:4584`. The session-id spelling probe already exists twice: `ResolveRetainedBinaryAsync` (as-sent, "D", "N") and `ComposeActiveDocumentEndpoints.ResolveSessionAsync` / `EnumerateSessionIdForms` (`Api/ComposeActiveDocumentEndpoints.cs:304-325`, private).
F4 POST /api/compose/document/{documentSpeId}/check-changes. Route at `Api/ComposeSyncEndpoints.cs:66`; handler `CheckDocumentChangesAsync` `:226-273`. It calls `SpeSyncOrchestrator.EnumerateChangesAsync(body.ContainerId)` immediately (`Services/Compose/SpeSyncOrchestrator.cs:232`, NOT virtual). That is an app-only Graph delta over any container (`SpeFileStore` `EnumerateDriveDeltaAsync` uses the app identity). It returns the named item's name, eTag and deleted flag, and it creates or advances the SHARED per-container delta state in Redis, which suppresses change detection for real users. The route declares produces 200/400/401/500 only, and `ComposeRouteSurfaceContractTests.cs:57` pins that list. Live client: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/useComposeWordShuttle.ts:~404-421`. Existing contract tests: `tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/ComposeWordShuttlePollEndpointContractTests.cs` (REAL SpeSyncOrchestrator over substituted dependencies).
F6 POST /api/compose/sessions/{sessionId}/annotations. Route at `Api/ComposeAnnotationEndpoints.cs:91`; handler `SaveAnnotations` `:360-389`. `.AddSessionOwnershipFilter()` authorizes (claim tid, sessionId); the handler then writes to (BODY tenantId `:372`, `:383`, sessionId). The sibling GET (`:309`, `:323`) was converted to the claim by task 059; the POST was not. `PullAnnotations` (`:118`, body.TenantId required at `:131`, used at `:134-135` in a log line only) and `ReanchorAnnotations` (`:212`, required at `:226`, log line `:230-231` only) also bind body.TenantId; read them at Step 0 to confirm it reaches no store key. Live client: `ComposeWorkspace.tsx:1540`.
GUARD STATE: all four files are already in `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.GovernedFiles` as `Scope.HandlerAuthorized` (`:300-337`), and the sweep found three of their reasons FALSE. ComposeDocumentEndpoints says "the handler resolves the caller and the document together", which is not true for promote. ComposeSyncEndpoints says "authenticated etag poll", with no handler check behind it. ComposeMountEndpoints says "/upload is content CREATION (no prior document)", but it is a read of another user's retained bytes.

══ DOCUMENTS (2 findings) ══
F0 PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}. Route and handler at `Api/DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs:95-162`. Gated `.AddDocumentAuthorizationFilter("write")` on the ROW only. It binds `Spaarke.Dataverse.UpdateDocumentRequest` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:322-556`), none of whose properties carry [JsonIgnore]. `DataverseServiceClientImpl.UpdateDocumentAsync` writes each one app-only when non-null. Two resource-naming groups matter:
 (a) SPE pointers: `GraphItemId` / `GraphDriveId` (`DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:822-826`) and `ParentGraphItemId`, `FilePath`. GET /{id}/download (`:238-385`) then streams `speFileStore.DownloadFileAsync(document.GraphDriveId, document.GraphItemId)` (`:315`) APP-ONLY. So a caller can repoint a row they can write at any SPE item, then download it as the managed identity.
 (b) Parent lookups, found while reviewing this POML (same route, same class, not named by the sweep): `EmailLookup`, `ParentDocumentLookup`, `MatterLookup`, `ProjectLookup`, `InvoiceLookup`, `WorkAssignmentLookup`, `EventLookup`, `TodoLookup`, `ContactLookup` are written as EntityReferences app-only (`DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:~922-975`). Nothing checks AppendTo on the target, so a caller can file a row they own under a secure matter they cannot see.
No client sends a PUT to /api/v1/documents/{id} (grep: 0 hits). `src/dataverse/webresources/spaarke_documents/DocumentOperations.js:103` declares the URL, but its upload flow writes the pointer columns through the FORM (`:417-428`), not through this PUT. The Copilot OpenAPI (`src/solutions/CopilotAgent/spaarke-bff-openapi.yaml:379`) declares GET only for this path. `UpdateDocumentRequest` is also built by server code (`Workers/Office/UploadFinalizationWorker.cs:632`, `:1215`, `Services/Ai/AppOnlyAnalysisService.cs:500`, `Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs:285`, `Services/Communication/MessageAttachmentMaterializer.cs:283`, `Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs:291`). Those set the C# properties directly and must keep working, so do not change the shared model's JSON contract. POST /api/v1/documents (the first hop of the sweep's chain) binds `CreateDocumentRequest` (`Models.cs:8-60`), which has no pointer property; it needs no change here.
⚠️ THE SAME CHAIN HAS A SECOND DOOR that the sweep did not name. Any user with Write on a sprk_document can set `sprk_graphdriveid` / `sprk_graphitemid` natively (MDA form, Xrm.WebApi); `DocumentOperations.js:417-428` does exactly that. The app-only download then follows them. Closing PUT alone does not close the chain. See escalation trigger 1.
F5 GET /api/v1/documents?containerId=. Handler at `Api/DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs:386-458`, bare `.RequireAuthorization()` at `:458`, app-only `GetDocumentsByContainerAsync` (`DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:1006-1024`) returning SPE pointers. With no containerId the handler returns 400 "ContainerId is required for listing documents" (`:419`) before any read. Its twin `GET /api/v1/containers/{containerId}/documents` (`:460+`) was gated by task 078 with `AddContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter`. The list route is latent today only because the handler requires `Guid.TryParse(containerId)` (`:411`) while real ids are "b!…" strings. It is hidden by a FALSE Permanent waiver: `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:578-581` ("COLLECTION READ … result trimming"), although the caller picks one container and no trimming exists. `NoWaiverIsStale` flags only PENDING waivers on gated routes (`:1033`), so a Permanent waiver left on a now-gated route will NOT fail the build; deleting it is this task's job. `ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter.cs`) reads the id from the ROUTE only (`:161`, `:227`); its missing-id branch returns the uniform 403 (`:231-242`). The only consumer is the Copilot agent OpenAPI (`spaarke-bff-openapi.yaml:349-375`, `listDocuments`), which declares a matterId parameter that the handler already rejects with 400; do not "fix" that here.

══ EXTERNAL ACCESS (1 finding) ══
F8 POST /api/v1/external-access/close-project. Route at `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:158`, on adminGroup (`:123-126`, `AddDelegationRuleFilter`). `Api/ExternalAccess/DelegationRuleFilter.cs:236-237` authorizes ONLY `CloseProjectRequest.ProjectId` (Write). The handler `ProjectClosureEndpoint.Handle` (`Api/ExternalAccess/ProjectClosureEndpoint.cs:79`) passes the body's free `string? ContainerId` (`Api/ExternalAccess/Dtos/CloseProjectRequest.cs:12`) to `SpeContainerMembershipService.RemoveAllExternalMembersAsync` (`:174-206`; the service method is virtual, `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/SpeContainerMembershipService.cs:335`). That method reads permissions app-only and deletes EVERY permission with a `GrantedToV2.User` (`:296-345`), internal users included. So the route is authorized against one id and mutates an unrelated container. The early return at `:128` (zero active grants) is not a guard, because a Write holder can create a grant. Live clients pass a containerId: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateProjectWizard/CloseProjectDialog.tsx:291-331` via `closureService.ts:20-71`, opened from LegalWorkspace `WorkspaceGrid.tsx:448`. Tests that construct `CloseProjectRequest` with a ContainerId: `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ProjectClosureCascadeTests.cs:255` and `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessIntegrationTests.cs:133`, `:462`, `:482`, `:545`, `:593`, `:885`.
SERVER DERIVATION ALREADY EXISTS: `RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync(entityLogicalName, recordId, ct)` (`Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs:142`; registered `Program.cs:63`; the class is `sealed` with non-virtual methods). Its decision (`SecureContainerDecision.cs`) yields ResolvedSecure (the record's OWN container), ResolvedFallback (the shared BUSINESS-UNIT container for a non-secure record), Unresolved, or FailClosed, and it can throw `SdapProblemException`. The precedent call with that catch is `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:632`. Task 085 is the precedent for deleting the client field and deriving from the authorized record. ⚠️ For a NON-secure project the derived container is the SHARED BU container, and clearing it would strip every user. `SpeContainerMembershipService.GrantMembershipAsync` (`:83`) has no BFF caller at authoring (grep). See escalation trigger 2.

══ FIELD MAPPINGS (1 finding) ══
F11 POST /api/v1/field-mappings/push. Route at `Api/FieldMappings/FieldMappingEndpoints.cs:60`; group `:24-27`; handler `PushFieldMappingsAsync` `:436-591`. It uses the app-only `IFieldMappingDataverseService` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IFieldMappingDataverseService.cs`, implemented by `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs`). Order today: profile query, then `RetrieveRecordFieldsAsync` on the source (`DataverseWebApiService.cs:921`), then up to 500 children via `QueryChildRecordIdsAsync` (`:975-1004`), then `UpdateRecordFieldsAsync` PATCHes on each child (`:1432`, which ALREADY accepts `Guid? impersonateSystemUserId`; the interface declares it at `IFieldMappingDataverseService.cs:43-48`). The route is latent today only because `DetermineParentLookupField` (`FieldMappingEndpoints.cs:671-678`) returns "_sprk_regarding{base}_value" and `QueryChildRecordIdsAsync` wraps it again (`DataverseWebApiService.cs:984`: `_{parentLookupField}_value`), so Dataverse answers 400 and the route returns 500. Whoever fixes that bug turns this into a critical mass write, so the guard and the bug fix land together, guard first. Live callers: `src/client/webresources/js/sprk_fieldmapping_push.js:148`, `src/client/webresources/js/sprk_updaterelated_commands.js:180`, `src/client/pcf/UpdateRelatedButton/UpdateRelatedButtonApp.tsx:161`. Tests: `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/FieldMappings/PushFieldMappingsTests.cs`, `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/FieldMappingEndpointsTests.cs:262-340`.
The impersonated read seam that already exists: `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.QueryAsync(entitySetName, odataQuery, callerSystemUserId, ct)` (`Services/Communication/IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.cs:21`). It passes through to `DataverseWebApiService.RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync` (`:1030`, refuses Guid.Empty), is registered unconditionally at `Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs:279`, and is already reused by Office and Workspace modules. The entity-set lookup is `IGenericEntityService.GetEntitySetNameAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs:67`).

══ OFFICE (1 finding) ══
F12 POST /api/office/quickcreate/{entityType}. Route at `Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs:1320-1327`; handler `QuickCreateAsync` `:1627-1715` parses the route value with `QuickCreateFieldRequirements.TryParse(entityType, …)` (`:~1661`). It calls `OfficeService.QuickCreateAsync` (`Services/Office/OfficeService.cs:1788-1880`): matter and project go through RecordCreationService, invoice through `IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync` (`:1865`). All are app-only creates. `AddQuickCreateSourceAccessFilter` (`Api/Filters/QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter.cs`, class `:~45-169`, Deny helper at the end) read-gates only the OPTIONAL source record and passes through when none is named. Nothing checks the caller's Create privilege on the target table. Only matter, project and invoice are created (`OfficeService.cs:1800-1809`); account and contact return null. The precedent is task 130 / owner G5: `CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync(token, privilegeName)` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:386`; OBO, WhoAmI, RetrieveUserSetOfPrivilegesByNames, uncached, fails closed, virtual), with the live-verified name `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.CreateInvoicePrivilege = "prvCreatesprk_Invoice"` (`Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:237`). The gap is recorded, unfixed, as caveat (2) of the OfficeEndpoints GovernedFile reason (`RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:207-222`). Live client: the Office add-in pane (`src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/`, EntityPicker quick-create). Existing tests that exercise the route: `tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeQuickCreateContractTests.cs`, `OfficeQuickCreateProjectContractTests.cs`, `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs`, `tests/integration/regression/Issue1079_InvoiceQuickCreateNameTests.cs`, `tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/OfficeRecordOwnershipTests.cs`.

══ REPORTING (3 findings) ══
F14 GET /api/reporting/embed-token (`Api/Reporting/ReportingEndpoints.cs:55`, handler `GetEmbedToken` `:157-221`), F15 POST /api/reporting/export (`:118`, handler `ExportReport` `:521-575`), F16 GET /api/reporting/reports/{reportId:guid} (`:76`, handler `GetReport` `:276-320`). Group (`:40-43`): RequireAuthorization plus `ReportingAuthorizationFilter`, which is a module gate plus the sprk_ReportingAccess role claim (`Api/Reporting/ReportingAuthorizationFilter.cs`). Nothing ties the caller-chosen workspaceId or reportId to the caller or to the catalog. `ReportingEmbedService` (`Api/Reporting/ReportingEmbedService.cs:23`, `public sealed class`, methods NOT virtual: `GetEmbedConfigAsync` `:119`, `GetReportAsync` `:356`, `ExportReportAsync` `:491`) uses the service principal with `profileId: null`. The catalog table `sprk_report` exists with `sprk_pbi_reportid` and `sprk_workspaceid`, BOTH declared as String attributes (MaxLength 100), not GUID columns (`scripts/Deploy-ReportingSchema.ps1:11-13`, `:341-358`). Its entity set is `sprk_reports` (`:743`). Viewer roles hold Org-scope Read on it (`:17-19`). RLS: `GetBusinessUnitRoles` (`ReportingEndpoints.cs:668-677`) reads a "businessunit"/"bu" claim that no Entra token or claims transformation produces, so tokens carry no BU role, contrary to `docs/guides/reporting-admin.md:384-389`. ⚠️ THE CLIENT/SERVER CONTRACT IS ALREADY BROKEN: the Reporting code page sends `reportId` WITHOUT workspaceId (`src/solutions/Reporting/src/services/reportingApi.ts:80-103` embed, `:142-160` export), while the BFF returns 400 without workspaceId (`ReportingEndpoints.cs:164-171`, `:284-291`, `:528-535`); the JSDoc there calls reportId "the sprk_report record GUID". The module maps only when `PowerBi:TenantId` is configured (`Api/Reporting/ReportingModule.cs:55-63`), which no checked-in appsettings sets. Tests: `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/Reporting/ReportingEndpointTests.cs:231-310`, `ReportingRlsTests.cs`; unit `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Reporting/ReportingEndpointsTests.cs` (calls handlers by reflection because the service is sealed, `:74-80`).
Caller-scoped Dataverse read for the catalog: `IDataverseUserClient.GetAsync(relativePath, ct)` (`Infrastructure/Dataverse/IDataverseUserClient.cs`; OBO only, no app-only fallback; general BFF infrastructure since task 126; registered `Infrastructure/DI/SpaarkeCore.cs:100`). Reference consumer: `Api/Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs` (task 127).

══ WORK ASSIGNMENTS (1 finding) ══
F1 POST /api/v1/work-assignments. Route at `Api/WorkAssignmentEndpoints.cs:29` (the file maps this one route only); group `:23-26`; handler `:45-138`. It does an app-only `IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync` with `ownerid` = the caller-chosen AssignedToUserId, so the record is user-owned, contrary to owner rounds 3b and 5 (records are team-owned via RecordOwnershipResolver). It also sends an app-authored notification with caller-controlled text to any user. It is broken today: GitHub #1035 (ISS-008) records that `sprk_matterid` / `sprk_duedate` do not exist on sprk_workassignment, so requests with MatterId or DueDate return 500. NO CLIENT: grep of src (excluding PCF bundle.js) for "api/v1/work-assignments" finds only the endpoint file. The "work-assignments" string elsewhere (PCF bundles, `external-spa/.../WorkAssignmentsWidget.tsx`, workspace section registrations) is a widget or EXTERNAL MODULE key (`/api/v1/external/...`), not this route; confirm in Step 0. Mapped at `Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:240`. Referenced by `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/InlineNotificationIntegrationPointsTests.cs:10`, `:71` (task 073 removed UploadEndpoints from the same list the same way). Task 158 inventories every BFF path that creates a work assignment; deleting this one removes a path from that inventory (notify 158 through the task note).

══ WORKSPACE STATE (1 finding) ══
F13 GET /api/workspace/state?sessionId=. Route at `Api/Workspace/WorkspaceStateEndpoints.cs:69`; group `:64-67`; handler `GetState` `:90-147`. It reads tid from the claim with its own lookup (`:~121`), then calls `IWorkspaceStateService.GetTabsAsync(tenantId, sessionId)` (Redis + Cosmos, keyed by the CHAT session id per `Services/Workspace/IWorkspaceStateService.cs:46`) with no owner binding. The store is write-dead since AIR2-075 (that project deliberately KEPT the route). No client calls it (only JSDoc in `Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/types/WorkspaceTab.ts`). The owner binding to reuse: `ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync(tenantId, sessionId)` (`Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs:223`, virtual; registered `Infrastructure/DI/AnalysisServicesModule.cs:428`) → `OwnerOid` (#863), exactly as `SessionOwnershipFilter.EvaluateAsync` (`Api/Filters/SessionOwnershipFilter.cs:110-175`, which also denies a null/empty OwnerOid) and the body-scoped handler check in `Api/ComposeActiveDocumentEndpoints.cs:95-124` do. An unknown session today answers 200 with an empty tab list. Existing tests: `tests/integration/contract/Api/Workspace/WorkspaceStateEndpointsContractTests.cs`.

══ THE GUARD ══
`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs` (task 074): `GovernedFiles` `:126-344` (Scope RouteLevelGate / HandlerAuthorized / GroupGated); `Waivers` `:378-`; a Pending waiver must name an owner, and a Permanent one is only for a genuine non-per-resource route. Rule A is `EveryGovernedRouteCarriesPerResourceAuthorizationOrANamedWaiver` (`:882`). `NoWaiverIsStale` (`:988-1060`) fails a PENDING waiver on a gated route and ANY waiver whose route no longer exists. Rule B is `NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative` (`:1107`) with `DecisionServices` (`:1274`) and `RuleBCoversEveryFilterRuleACredits` (`:1674`). `FilterMarker` + `ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames` are at `:1886-1902`; `.Add…AuthorizationFilter(` names are credited automatically, and `QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter` is credited by name. The endpoint-file census is `ExpectedEndpointFileCount = 120` (`:875`), with a per-change history comment above it. Task 167 (NOT authored and NOT on this branch on 2026-10-03) extends this guard to every route file and adds a Pending waiver owned by this task for each of the 17 routes. Of the files in scope, only DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs, OfficeEndpoints.cs and the four Compose files are governed today.

══ REUSE, DO NOT FORK (each read for this POML) ══
• `CallerRecordAccessProbe` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs`): `GetCallerRightsAsync(token, entitySet, recordId)` `:212` (OBO WhoAmI + RetrievePrincipalAccess; None on every fault; a ~1.6 s not-found backoff `:101-106` that also lands on records the caller cannot see), `GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync` `:274`, `GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` `:342` (null = do not proceed), `CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync` `:386`. All are virtual, which is the ADR-038 test seam. Registered `Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:122`.
• `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs`; extension `:24-36`, class `:79-233`): reads route values `{entityLogicalName}` / `{recordId}` (`:105-108`), resolves `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (a miss DENIES, reasonCode `entity_type_not_authorizable`), calls the probe, then `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights`, and returns 403 via `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden`. Its rights-deny detail (`:221-224`, reasonCode `insufficient_rights`) is upload-specific ("add content to this record").
• `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:174`, internal static; map `:115-147` holds contact, sprk_matter/matter, sprk_project/project, sprk_invoice/invoice, sprk_workassignment/workassignment, sprk_event/event, sprk_todo/todo; LOCKSTEP with DocumentAssociationMap, so never add entries).
• `ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter` (task 078): container → owning record (`RecordContainerResolver.ResolveOwningRecordAsync`) → caller Read via `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync`; refuses ownerless containers; one uniform 403 (`errorCode` `container_documents_access_denied`).
• `SessionOwnershipFilter` (`Api/Filters/SessionOwnershipFilter.cs`) and the body-scoped in-handler pattern (`ComposeActiveDocumentEndpoints.cs:95-124`, "not-yours and not-found are deliberately the same answer"); `SessionOwnershipGuardTests.BodyScopedSessionRoutes` (a documented list; each row needs a reason and an existing file).
• OBO SPE visibility probe: `SpeFileStore.GetFileMetadataAsUserAsync(httpContext, driveId, itemId)` (`Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs:130-135`, NOT virtual); precedent "visibleToCaller" at `Services/Compose/ComposePdfIntakeCoordinator.cs:358`. `SpeFileStore.ResolveDriveIdAsync` (`:211-`, NOT virtual; returns a "b!" id unchanged without Graph).
• `RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync` (above). `IDataverseUserClient` (above). `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.QueryAsync` (above). `TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId(User)` and `CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId(User)` (`Infrastructure/Authentication/`). `ProblemDetailsHelper.ValidationError(detail)` and `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden(reasonCode, detail, traceId)` (`Infrastructure/Errors/`). `OperationAccessPolicy` keys: "read" = Read, "write" = Write, "entity.associate_document" = AppendTo (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs:163-275`).</background>
