  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every route touched. Fail closed. A missing caller oid, a missing bearer token, an unresolvable Dataverse user, an OBO exchange failure, a RetrievePrincipalAccess or privilege-query fault, a session-store fault, or any exception inside the decision DENIES. There is no app-only fallback on any decision path. A try/catch around a decision covers the decision only, never the handler body (the task-072 rule in RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:196-211).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / ADR-019">Scope: every deny added. An unknown target and a forbidden target get the SAME status, title, detail, reasonCode and extension keys on that route. Never echo whether the target exists. Every deny carries a machine-readable reasonCode. The deny on each route is exactly:
 • F7 memory records → the RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter 403 (reasonCode `insufficient_rights`, the memory-specific detail "You do not have access to this record, so its memory cannot be read.").
 • F9/F10 pins → 403 via `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden("insufficient_rights", "You do not have permission to pin content to this matter.", traceId)`.
 • F3 Compose upload → the existing 404 "Uploaded File Not Available" (same title and detail as today's expired-bytes answer).
 • F4 check-changes → 404, title "Document Not Found", detail "The document was not found or you do not have access to it.", reasonCode `sdap.compose.deny.document_not_visible`.
 • F5 documents list → the ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter 403 the twin route already returns.
 • F11 field-mappings push → the existing 404 "Source Record Not Found", with the detail changed to "Source record not found." (no id, no entity name).
 • F12 quick-create → 403 in the QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter.Deny shape (errorCode OFFICE_009, reasonCode `insufficient_privilege`, correlationId).
 • F14-F16 reporting → 404, title "Report Not Found", reasonCode `sdap.reporting.deny.report_not_in_catalog`.
 • F13 workspace state → the existing unknown-session answer (200, tabs [], activeTabId null, userSelection null).
A fault in the decision (probe throws, store throws) may use the route's existing fault reasonCode (`access_check_failed` on the filters) but must never reach the downstream service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugins. Every check lives in the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: the fix pattern. Reads: the caller's OWN Dataverse rights decide (D1, C9), through CallerRecordAccessProbe (RetrievePrincipalAccess as the caller), IDataverseUserClient (OBO), or the impersonated read seam. Writes: a rights pre-check as the user, then an app-only write only where a server invariant needs it (the 130 / 146 G5 pattern); otherwise the write runs as the user (impersonated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. No new filter class, no new service, no new enum, no new logical-name → entity-set map, and no entries added to EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType or SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets. Extend instead: RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter gains an optional `string? denyDetail = null` argument on the extension and ctor (null keeps today's text); ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter gains an optional `string? queryParameter = null` argument on the extension (null keeps the route-value behaviour); QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter gains the target-table Create-privilege check. Exactly ONE OperationAccessPolicy key is added: "memory.pin_matter" = AppendTo, with the three-question justification in the PR, and OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests gains its InlineData rows (call-site discovery and least-privilege resolution). Making SpeFileStore.GetFileMetadataAsUserAsync / ResolveDriveIdAsync virtual and unsealing ReportingEmbedService (methods GetEmbedConfigAsync, GetReportAsync, ExportReportAsync made virtual) are permitted ADR-010 test seams, stated in the note. Any other new type needs the three-question justification with grep evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F7 memory records. Rename the route parameter `{id:guid}` to `{recordId:guid}` (the URL is unchanged) and rename the handler parameter to match. Attach `.AddRecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter("read", denyDetail: "You do not have access to this record, so its memory cannot be read.")` to that route's own fluent chain, so the decision is Read on the exact record, as the caller, before the handler. `MemoryAccessAuthorizer.CanCallerReadRecordAsync` stays in the handler as-is (it can only narrow), but the filter is the decision. A subjectType outside EntityAccessFilter's map is DENIED by the filter's existing miss rule. This is decided: `sprk_document` record memory (written by ComposeMemoryCapturer.cs:103) becomes unreadable through this route. It is the fail-closed outcome on a route with no client, and it is recorded in the note, not escalated (unless a caller is found; see escalation trigger 3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F9/F10 pins. This applies to EVERY pinType, not only matter-fact. Whenever a create or update request carries a non-blank MatterId:
 • it must parse as a GUID, else 400 (field-level ProblemDetails) with no probe call;
 • the caller must hold AppendTo on sprk_matters(matterId), per CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync(TokenHelper.ExtractBearerTokenOrNull(httpContext), entitySet, matterId) with the entity set from EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet("sprk_matter") and the decision from OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights(rights, "memory.pin_matter");
 • the check runs BEFORE repository.CreateAsync / UpdateAsync.
AppendTo was decided at authoring: a pin is injected into every other user's prompt for that matter (ContextBinder.cs:864-872, :917), which is attaching content to the matter, the same right "entity.associate_document" demands for a document. On PUT, the matter check runs on the NEW MatterId in the body, every time one is present. The existing pin lookup (404) and pin-ownership check (403) stay and run first. A request with no MatterId is unchanged (user-preference pins). The stored MatterId string is the value as sent (no reformatting), so existing pins keep matching. Add `.ProducesProblem(StatusCodes.Status403Forbidden)` to POST /pins.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F2 promote and F1 work-assignments. DELETE the route, its handler, the request/response types used only by it, and its mapping, after proving zero callers. The proof is a grep of src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,cs,yaml} excluding bin/obj/dist/node_modules and PCF bundle.js; record the commands and results in the note. Keep `IComposeService.PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` and `PromoteComposeDocumentRequest` (used by create-on-save). Delete or rewrite the tests that exercised the deleted routes: ComposeRouteSurfaceContractTests.cs:65, the PostPromoteDocument_* tests in ComposeEndpointsContractTests.cs, and the WorkAssignmentEndpoints reference in InlineNotificationIntegrationPointsTests.cs (follow the task-073 precedent in that file's remarks). Add an absence guard in tests/integration/regression/RouteAuthorization/DeadRouteRetirementTests.cs that maps the real endpoints and asserts both routes answer 404 or 405 (the DriveKeyedWriteRouteRetirementTests precedent, task 083). Deleting WorkAssignmentEndpoints.cs changes the endpoint-file census: update ExpectedEndpointFileCount (RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:875) and add a history line above it in the same diff. If a caller IS found for either route, do not delete it; fire escalation trigger 3.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F3 Compose upload. Before any cache read, resolve the chat session named by body.SessionId under the CLAIM tenant (TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId) with ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync. Try the spellings in the order ComposeActiveDocumentEndpoints.EnumerateSessionIdForms uses (as-sent, "N", "D"); copy that private helper's logic into the handler, or move it to an internal static method one of the two existing files exposes, and do not create a new class. The first session found must have a non-empty OwnerOid equal (ordinal) to CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId(User). Not owned, null/empty OwnerOid, not found, or a store fault → the existing 404 "Uploaded File Not Available"; ITenantCache is not read, and IComposeService.ProjectForMount is not called (so no projection is built and no PDF-source marker is written). Add "Api/ComposeMountEndpoints.cs" to SessionOwnershipGuardTests.BodyScopedSessionRoutes with a reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F4 check-changes. Before EnumerateChangesAsync: resolve driveId = SpeFileStore.ResolveDriveIdAsync(body.ContainerId), then require SpeFileStore.GetFileMetadataAsUserAsync(httpContext, driveId, documentSpeId) to return non-null (OBO: the caller can see THIS item in THIS drive). Null, an exception, or an unresolvable container → the F4 404, and SpeSyncOrchestrator.EnumerateChangesAsync is never called. No Redis delta or eTag state is created or advanced, and no container is added to the tracked index. Add `.Produces(StatusCodes.Status404NotFound)` to the route and update its pinned line in ComposeRouteSurfaceContractTests.cs (:57) to produces=200,400,401,404,500. The response shape for an authorized caller is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F6 annotations, and every other handler in ComposeAnnotationEndpoints.cs. The tenant used for any store key, cache key, ChatSession lookup or log line is TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId(User). On SaveAnnotations a missing tid claim is already a 401 from SessionOwnershipFilter; on PullAnnotations and ReanchorAnnotations a missing tid claim → 401 with no download. body.TenantId is neither required nor read on all three handlers: remove the three "tenantId is required in the request body" 400s, keep the DTO property (so the shipped client's payload still binds), and mark it obsolete in its XML doc. Update any existing test that asserted those 400s.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F0 PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}. Refuse, with ProblemDetailsHelper.ValidationError naming the field(s), any request body in which ANY of these UpdateDocumentRequest properties is non-null: GraphDriveId, GraphItemId, ParentGraphItemId, FilePath, EmailLookup, ParentDocumentLookup, MatterLookup, ProjectLookup, InvoiceLookup, WorkAssignmentLookup, EventLookup, TodoLookup, ContactLookup. The check runs in the handler BEFORE the handler's GetDocumentAsync and before UpdateDocumentAsync, so the row is unchanged. Do this in the endpoint (a check on the bound request object), NOT by adding [JsonIgnore] to Spaarke.Dataverse.UpdateDocumentRequest: the shared model is built by the server code listed in the background, and its JSON contract must not change. Re-filing a document is not this route's job and has no client here. The native-write door (MDA / Xrm.WebApi) is escalation trigger 1, not a silent scope cut.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F5 GET /api/v1/documents?containerId=. Gate it with `.AddContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter(queryParameter: "containerId")` in its own chain (the twin route keeps calling it with no argument). When the query source is declared and the parameter is absent or blank, the filter returns ProblemDetailsHelper.ValidationError("ContainerId is required for listing documents") itself, with no resolver or Dataverse call; it must NOT call next() for a missing id. The route-source missing-id branch keeps its uniform 403. Do not fix the Guid.TryParse type bug at :411 in this task (task 078's note §4 owns it); the gate must hold whatever that bug's state. DELETE the Permanent waiver "GET /api/v1/documents" (RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:578-581). The route then passes Rule A as gated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F8 close-project. DELETE `ContainerId` from CloseProjectRequest (task 085 precedent). First confirm that the BFF's JSON options skip unknown members (System.Text.Json default UnmappedMemberHandling.Skip; a grep of src/server for "UnmappedMemberHandling" at authoring found no Disallow on the request pipeline), so the shipped client's containerId still binds and is ignored. The handler takes RecordContainerResolver and derives the container with ResolveForRecordAsync("sprk_project", request.ProjectId, ct), after the zero-active-grants early return and only on the path that today reaches the container step:
 • ResolvedSecure with a non-blank ContainerId → that container is the ONLY one RemoveAllExternalMembersAsync may be called with;
 • ResolvedFallback or Unresolved → the container step is skipped (never called with the shared BU container), containerCleared stays true, and the note records the outcome in the log line;
 • FailClosed, a blank container on ResolvedSecure, an SdapProblemException or any other resolver exception → containerCleared = false, which yields the existing ClosureIncomplete 500 (ClosureContainerNotClearedReason). Dataverse grant deactivation still runs as today.
The DelegationRuleFilter Write gate on ProjectId is unchanged. The client files closureService.ts and CloseProjectDialog.tsx may keep sending containerId; removing it client-side is optional and, if done, ships with this PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F11 field-mappings push.
 (a) Source: before the profile query, the source read, the child query or any write, resolve the entity set with EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet(request.SourceEntity) and require Read on the source record as the caller (CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync; OperationAccessPolicy "read"). A denied source, an unknown id, an unmapped SourceEntity, a missing token or a probe fault → the identical F11 404. The validation 400s for malformed requests stay first.
 (b) Children: resolve the caller's systemuserid with CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync; null → the same 404 with nothing read. Query child ids AS THE CALLER through IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.QueryAsync(entitySet, odataQuery, callerSystemUserId, ct), where entitySet = IGenericEntityService.GetEntitySetNameAsync(request.TargetEntity) and odataQuery = `$filter=_sprk_regarding{base}_value eq {sourceRecordId}&amp;$select={target}id&amp;$top={MaxChildRecordsPerPush + 1}`. The `_…_value` wrapping is applied exactly ONCE ({base} is SourceEntity without the "sprk_" prefix, as DetermineParentLookupField computes it today), and {sourceRecordId} is the bound Guid formatted "D". Write each child with UpdateRecordFieldsAsync(…, impersonateSystemUserId: callerSystemUserId). Children the caller cannot Read never appear in the response (not in TotalRecords, Errors or FieldResults).
 (c) Do NOT edit src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs or IFieldMappingDataverseService.cs (project rule: parallel-unsafe); the seams above already exist. The handler stops calling QueryChildRecordIdsAsync, which removes the double prefix together with the guard.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner G5 / task 130">Scope: F12 quick-create. In QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter, read the route value "entityType" and parse it with QuickCreateFieldRequirements.TryParse (the parser the handler uses). For Matter, Project and Invoice only, require CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync(TokenHelper.ExtractBearerTokenOrNull(httpContext), privilege) to return true BEFORE next(): Matter → the live-verified prvCreatesprk_Matter name, Project → the live-verified prvCreatesprk_Project name, Invoice → FinanceAuthorizationFilter.CreateInvoicePrivilege (reuse the constant, do not retype it). The matter and project privilege names are read from live metadata (`privileges?$filter=name eq '…'`, read-only) and recorded in the note BEFORE they are written into code, and each constant is pinned by a test naming the live value. false, a throw or no token → the F12 403. An unparseable entityType and Account / Contact pass through to the handler unchanged (its 400 or its existing answer). The existing source-record Read check is unchanged and runs first; its pass-through when no source is named now applies only to the source half. The create stays app-only and team-owned (the server invariant G5 keeps). Rewrite caveat (2) of the OfficeEndpoints GovernedFile reason (RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:219-222) to say the Create privilege is now checked for matter, project and invoice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F14/F15/F16 reporting. Before any ReportingEmbedService call, and after the existing 400s for a missing workspaceId or reportId, read the sprk_report catalog AS THE CALLER through IDataverseUserClient.GetAsync with `sprk_reports?$select=sprk_reportid&amp;$filter=sprk_pbi_reportid eq '{reportId}' and sprk_workspaceid eq '{workspaceId}'&amp;$top=1`. Both columns are String attributes, so the values are quoted string literals; {reportId} and {workspaceId} are the bound Guid values formatted lowercase "D" (never raw request text). No row (absent OR unreadable; Dataverse answers both as empty), a non-success status, an OBO failure or any fault → the identical F14-F16 404, and ReportingEmbedService is not invoked. Before writing this, verify read-only and record in the note: the entity set name, the two column names and types (EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_report')), and the stored format of the two values on existing rows. Keep the existing workspaceId + reportId request contract. Do NOT redesign RLS or the client contract in this task (escalation trigger 5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: F13 workspace state. Before GetTabsAsync, resolve ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync(TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId(User), sessionId) and require a non-empty OwnerOid equal (ordinal) to CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId(User). Not owned, null/empty OwnerOid, not found, or a store fault → the unknown-session answer (200, empty tabs), and GetTabsAsync is NOT called. Confirm at Step 0 that ChatSessionManager's registration (AnalysisServicesModule.cs:428) is unconditional; if it is inside a feature flag, the route needs the same condition (CLAUDE.md §10 F.1). Add "Api/Workspace/WorkspaceStateEndpoints.cs" to SessionOwnershipGuardTests.BodyScopedSessionRoutes with a reason stating that the id arrives in the QUERY. Do not delete the route (AIR2-075 kept it deliberately).</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 074 / task 167 (owner round 9 item 3)">Scope: RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs. First check whether task 167 has landed on this branch (a tasks/167-*.poml exists AND RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs carries Pending waivers whose owner is "166").
 (a) If 167 HAS landed: for each of the 17 routes, delete the Pending waiver 167 added. That includes waivers keyed on routes this task deletes (promote, work-assignments) and the F7 waiver keyed "{id:guid}", which the rename makes ABSENT. Make each surviving route pass 167's per-resource rule. Prefer the route-level filter visible in the fluent chain; a handler-level check is acceptable only where the authorization subject is a body/query session id or a body id that no existing filter can read, and then the file's classification must say so.
 (b) If 167 has NOT landed: do not add GovernedFiles entries for any file that is not governed today. DO make the edits for files already governed: delete the "GET /api/v1/documents" Permanent waiver; rewrite the three false Compose HandlerAuthorized reasons (ComposeDocumentEndpoints without promote, ComposeSyncEndpoints, ComposeMountEndpoints) to describe the checks this task adds; rewrite the OfficeEndpoints caveat (2); update ExpectedEndpointFileCount. Then write, in the task note, a per-route table: route → mechanism (filter name or handler check) → the classification and waiver 167 must NOT add (or must delete). The main session reconciles at integration.
In both cases every filter used must stay credited by FilterMarker (:1886-1902) AND inspected by Rule B (NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative :1107; RuleBCoversEveryFilterRuleACredits :1674). Do not change FilterMarker, DecisionServices or ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute at existing seams: CallerRecordAccessProbe's virtual methods, IDataverseUserClient, IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery, IFieldMappingDataverseService, IGenericEntityService, ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync (virtual), ITenantCache, IComposeService, IMemoryItemStore, IPinnedContextRepository, IWorkspaceStateService, SpeContainerMembershipService.RemoveAllExternalMembersAsync (virtual), IDocumentDataverseService. RecordContainerResolver is sealed: construct the REAL resolver over substituted ISecurableEntityRegistry and IGenericEntityService, as tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/RecordContainerResolverTests.cs does. SpeSyncOrchestrator.EnumerateChangesAsync is not virtual: assert "never invoked" on the dependencies beneath the real orchestrator (the ComposeWordShuttlePollEndpointContractTests setup). For SpeFileStore and ReportingEmbedService use the permitted virtual seams (constraint above). Host the REAL Map*Endpoints in-process (the FinanceRollupEndpointsContractTests pattern). No live Dataverse, Graph, Cosmos or Power BI in CI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: every new check. Prove it bites by seeding: remove or invert the check locally, run its tests, confirm that at least one FAILS naming the route, then restore. Record each seeding result in the note (the 130 §11.4 practice). A check whose removal turns nothing red is not done.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project hard gate">Scope: before the PR. Run the affected tests, the FULL BFF unit suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests, which also compiles tests/integration/{contract,auth,regression,seam}), the NetArchTest suite (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests), and BOTH integration suites IN FULL with `dotnet test`: tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests AND tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests. A build alone does not count (project CLAUDE.md, batch-3 lesson). Record the pass/skip/fail counts in the note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF: existing routes, no new service) citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md. Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master from a SHORT path (for example C:\wt166m and C:\wt166b), both sides zipped with Compress-Archive, with equal file counts. Report both absolute sizes and the delta; the ceiling is 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH. Run /conflict-check before the PR (Compose files: spaarkeai-compose-r8; Office files: spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/r2; Api/ExternalAccess: SPA-external-access r1/r2/r3 and teams-app-r1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 / round 9 (binding)">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred: scope found during execution is added to this task or raised through an escalation trigger, never dropped. Live Dataverse, Cosmos, SPE and Power BI are READ-ONLY during development; every live write is a manual gate run by the main session.</constraint>
  </constraints>

