  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Read the evidence file (project copy first; see the background). Re-verify every anchor in the background against current source. Check whether task 167 has landed (the guard constraint's test) and record which branch applies. Run the zero-caller greps for promote, work-assignments, memory/records and PUT /api/v1/documents, and record the commands and results. Read ComposeAnnotationEndpoints' pull/reanchor handlers to confirm body.TenantId reaches only log lines. Confirm ChatSessionManager's registration is unconditional.</step>
    <step order="1">Read-only live checks, recorded in the note before any constant is written: the privilege names for Create on sprk_matter and sprk_project; sprk_report's entity set, column names, types and stored value format; for each active field-mapping profile, its source entity (is it in EntityAccessFilter's map?) and whether its target table carries `sprk_regarding{base}` for its source; which record-memory subjectTypes exist in Cosmos (a count query, read-only); whether dev's BFF app user holds prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser (role lookup, not a call); whether the Reporting module is configured in dev; whether field-level security covers sprk_graphdriveid / sprk_graphitemid (fieldpermission rows), as input to escalation trigger 1.</step>
    <step order="2">Memory: F7 (route parameter rename + RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter "read" with the memory deny detail); F9/F10 (MatterId GUID validation + "memory.pin_matter" AppendTo check on create and on update's new MatterId, every pinType); the OperationAccessPolicy key and its completeness rows.</step>
    <step order="3">Compose: delete promote (F2) with its tests; session-owner check on upload (F3); OBO item check before the delta, plus the 404 produce (F4); claim tenant in every annotation handler (F6); the SessionOwnershipGuardTests row for ComposeMountEndpoints.cs.</step>
    <step order="4">Documents: refuse the thirteen resource-naming fields on PUT (F0); extend ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter with the query source and gate the list route (F5); delete the Permanent waiver.</step>
    <step order="5">Close-project: delete ContainerId from the DTO; derive via RecordContainerResolver; only ResolvedSecure clears (F8); update the tests that construct the DTO.</step>
    <step order="6">Field-mappings push: source Read gate; impersonated child query (single `_…_value` wrap) and impersonated child writes; unreadable children absent from the response (F11).</step>
    <step order="7">Office quick-create: target-table Create privilege in QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter (F12); update the GovernedFile caveat; give the existing quick-create tests a privilege-granting probe.</step>
    <step order="8">Reporting: caller-scoped catalog binding before every Power BI call on embed-token, export and reports/{reportId} (F14-F16); the ReportingEmbedService test seam.</step>
    <step order="9">Work assignments: delete the route and file (F1), update the census count and history line, add the absence guard. Workspace state: session-owner binding (F13) and its SessionOwnershipGuardTests row.</step>
    <step order="10">Guard reconciliation per the guard constraint (branch a or b), with the per-route table in the note.</step>
    <step order="11">Tests for the closed set below; seeding proof for every new check; full test runs (both integration suites in full); publish size; CVE check; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="12">Write notes/task-166-memory-compose-remaining-route-authorization.md: findings appendix, live read-only facts, seeding results, guard table, test counts, publish size, escalations fired, and the note to task 158. Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` only when every testable criterion is met. The manual live gate stays pending for the main session.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">F7 GET /api/memory/records/{entityLogicalName}/{recordId}: the route carries `.AddRecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter("read", …)` in its own fluent chain. A caller the probe reports as None on that record, and separately a record id that does not exist, get the identical 403 (reasonCode insufficient_rights, the memory detail), and IMemoryItemStore.GetForRecordAsync is never called. An entityLogicalName not in EntityAccessFilter's map (test with "sprk_document") gets 403 with no probe and no store call. A caller with Read gets 200 with that record's items. No bearer token, or a throwing probe, → 403 with no store call. The probe is asked about the exact entity set and recordId from the route (asserted on the seam arguments). Tested through the real MapMemoryGovernanceEndpoints host.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F9 POST /api/memory/pins: a request with a non-blank MatterId the caller lacks AppendTo on, and separately a non-existent matter id, get the identical 403 and IPinnedContextRepository.CreateAsync is never called. This holds for pinType matter-fact AND for a user-preference pin carrying a MatterId. A non-GUID MatterId → 400 with no probe call. A caller with AppendTo → 201 as today. A request with no MatterId → 201 with no probe call. The probe is asked about entity set sprk_matters and the body's MatterId (asserted on the seam arguments). A caller holding Read and Write but not AppendTo is denied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F10 PUT /api/memory/pins/{pinId}: the caller's own pin re-pointed at a matter the caller lacks AppendTo on → 403, and IPinnedContextRepository.UpdateAsync is never called. The check is made on the NEW MatterId in the body, not the stored one (asserted on the seam arguments). A pin owned by another user still gets the existing 403, and no probe call is made for it. An unknown pin still gets the existing 404. An owned pin with an authorized new MatterId → 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F2 POST /api/compose/documents/{documentSpeId}/promote no longer exists. DeadRouteRetirementTests maps the real Compose endpoints and the route answers 404 or 405. ComposeRouteSurfaceContractTests no longer lists it. PromoteComposeDocumentBody and PromoteComposeDocumentResponse are gone. IComposeService.PromoteIfEphemeralAsync still exists and the create-on-save tests that use it stay green. The note records the zero-caller grep.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F3 POST /api/compose/upload: a session owned by another user in the same tenant gets the identical 404 "Uploaded File Not Available" that a missing session gets. This is tested for each id spelling the client could send (as-sent, "D", "N"), for a session with a null OwnerOid, and for a store fault in the session lookup. In every one of those cases ITenantCache is never read for "doc-upload-binary" and IComposeService.ProjectForMount is never called. The caller's own session → 200 as today. ComposeMountEndpoints.cs is listed in SessionOwnershipGuardTests.BodyScopedSessionRoutes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F4 POST /api/compose/document/{documentSpeId}/check-changes: when GetFileMetadataAsUserAsync returns null, and separately when it throws, and when the container cannot be resolved, the response is the identical F4 404, and SpeSyncOrchestrator.EnumerateChangesAsync never runs (asserted on the dependencies beneath the real orchestrator, so no delta state is created or advanced). A caller who can see the item gets 200 with the unchanged response shape. The route declares 404 and ComposeRouteSurfaceContractTests pins produces=200,400,401,404,500 for it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F6 POST /api/compose/sessions/{sessionId}/annotations: with a body tenantId different from the claim tid, IComposeService.SaveComposeAnnotationsAsync receives the CLAIM tenant, and no call carries the body tenant. A body with no tenantId → 200 (no longer 400). For PullAnnotations and ReanchorAnnotations: a body with no tenantId is no longer refused, a missing tid claim → 401 with no download, and the note records that body.TenantId reached only log lines (or, if it reached a store, a test asserts the claim tenant is used there).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F0 PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}: for each of the thirteen refused properties (GraphDriveId, GraphItemId, ParentGraphItemId, FilePath and the nine *Lookup properties), a body carrying only that property → 400 naming it, and IDocumentDataverseService.UpdateDocumentAsync is never called (thirteen cases, a theory is fine). A body with only permitted fields (for example Name), from a caller with Write → 200 as today. A caller without Write still gets the existing document-filter deny. Spaarke.Dataverse.UpdateDocumentRequest has no new [JsonIgnore] (the diff shows src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F5 GET /api/v1/documents?containerId=: the route carries `.AddContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter(queryParameter: "containerId")` in its own chain. A container whose owning record the caller cannot Read, and separately a container with no establishable owner, get the same 403 the twin route GET /api/v1/containers/{containerId}/documents returns, and GetDocumentsByContainerAsync is never called. No containerId → 400 "ContainerId is required for listing documents" with no resolver or Dataverse call. The twin route's behaviour is unchanged (its existing tests stay green). The Permanent waiver "GET /api/v1/documents" is deleted and Rule A passes for the route as gated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F8 POST /api/v1/external-access/close-project: CloseProjectRequest has no ContainerId. A request whose JSON carries a "containerId" of another container never causes RemoveAllExternalMembersAsync to be called with that value (asserted on the seam). For a project the real resolver reports ResolvedSecure, RemoveAllExternalMembersAsync is called exactly once, with the project's own container. For ResolvedFallback or Unresolved it is never called and the response is 200. For FailClosed, and separately for a resolver SdapProblemException, the response is the existing ClosureIncomplete 500 with ClosureContainerNotClearedReason, and the grant deactivation still ran. A caller without Write on ProjectId still gets the existing DelegationRuleFilter deny, with no resolver call. ExternalAccessIntegrationTests and ProjectClosureCascadeTests compile and pass against the new DTO.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F11 POST /api/v1/field-mappings/push: a caller the probe reports as None on the source, and separately an unknown source id, a SourceEntity not in EntityAccessFilter's map, and a missing token, get the identical F11 404, and no profile query, source read, child query or write happens. The child query is issued through IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.QueryAsync with the caller's systemuserid, and its filter attribute is exactly `_sprk_regarding{base}_value` (a test pins the string, so the double prefix cannot return). Every child write passes impersonateSystemUserId = the caller's systemuserid, so no app-only child write remains. A child the impersonated query does not return is absent from TotalRecords, Errors and FieldResults. GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync returning null → the same 404 with nothing read. IFieldMappingDataverseService.QueryChildRecordIdsAsync is no longer called by the handler. DataverseWebApiService.cs and IFieldMappingDataverseService.cs are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F12 POST /api/office/quickcreate/{entityType}: for each of matter, project and invoice, a caller for whom CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync returns false, and separately one for whom it throws, and a request with no bearer token, get 403 (OFFICE_009, reasonCode insufficient_privilege, correlationId), and neither IOfficeService.QuickCreateAsync nor IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync is invoked. The privilege name asked for equals the live-verified constant pinned by a test; invoice reuses FinanceAuthorizationFilter.CreateInvoicePrivilege. A caller holding the privilege gets 201 as today. Account, contact and an invalid entityType get the same responses as before this task, with no privilege query. When a source is named and unreadable, the existing source-record Read deny still fires, and no privilege query is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F14 GET /api/reporting/embed-token, F15 POST /api/reporting/export, F16 GET /api/reporting/reports/{reportId}: when the caller-context catalog query returns no sprk_report row for (workspaceId, reportId), and separately when the OBO read fails or returns a non-success status, each route returns the identical 404 (reasonCode sdap.reporting.deny.report_not_in_catalog), and ReportingEmbedService is never invoked. The catalog query goes through IDataverseUserClient (never an app-only client). Its path names the live-verified entity set and filters on both live-verified columns as quoted lowercase "D" GUID strings (a test pins the path). A catalogued pair returns 200 as today. The existing 400s for a missing workspaceId or reportId, and the module-gate and role responses, are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F1 POST /api/v1/work-assignments no longer exists. Api/WorkAssignmentEndpoints.cs and its mapping line are deleted. DeadRouteRetirementTests asserts the route answers 404 or 405. ExpectedEndpointFileCount is updated in the same diff, with a history line, and the census test passes. InlineNotificationIntegrationPointsTests no longer references the deleted type. The note records the zero-caller grep and tells task 158 that this create path is gone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">F13 GET /api/workspace/state: a sessionId whose chat session is owned by another user, and separately a session with a null OwnerOid, a sessionId with no chat session, and a session-store fault, all return the identical unknown-session answer (200, empty tabs, activeTabId null, userSelection null), and IWorkspaceStateService.GetTabsAsync is never called. The owner's session returns its tabs as today. WorkspaceStateEndpoints.cs is listed in SessionOwnershipGuardTests.BodyScopedSessionRoutes, with a reason naming the query parameter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Filter reach: for every route whose decision is an endpoint filter (F5, F7, F12), a test through the REAL Map*Endpoints host proves that a None caller is denied on that route. A test that invokes the filter class directly does not satisfy this criterion. RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter's default deny text, the twin container route's behaviour and QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter's source-half behaviour are unchanged (their existing tests stay green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Guard: if task 167 has landed, no Pending waiver owned by this task remains for any of the 17 routes (including the deleted routes and the renamed F7 key), and every surviving route passes 167's rule. If it has not, the note carries the per-route mechanism table and the already-governed edits are made: the GET /api/v1/documents Permanent waiver is deleted; the three Compose HandlerAuthorized reasons and OfficeEndpoints caveat (2) are rewritten to match the code. In both cases Rule A, Rule B, RuleBCoversEveryFilterRuleACredits, the census and NoWaiverIsStale pass, and FilterMarker, DecisionServices and ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding: for each new check (F0, F3, F4, F5, F6, F7, F8, F9, F10, F11 source, F11 children, F12, F13, F14-F16), removing it locally turns at least one of this task's tests red, naming the route. Each result is recorded in the note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new logical-name → entity-set map exists. EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType and SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets are unchanged (the diff shows no entries added). DataverseWebApiService.cs, IFieldMappingDataverseService.cs and Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs are unchanged. OperationAccessPolicy gains exactly one key, "memory.pin_matter" = AppendTo, and OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests pass with its rows.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover exactly the behaviours above plus the fail-closed branches named in the constraints; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the note. The ADR-038 bans are respected (no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The BFF build is green. The affected tests, the full BFF unit suite, NetArchTest, and BOTH integration suites (Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and Spe.Integration.Tests) run in full and are green, with counts recorded. Publish size is reported against a fresh origin/master build per CLAUDE.md §10 (both absolute sizes, delta, zip tool, equal file counts) and is ≤60 MB. No new HIGH CVE. /conflict-check has been run and its result recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, run by the main session after deploy, using existing non-admin test users in their current BU; ids redacted to 8 characters in the note):
(a) a user with no access to matter M gets 403 on GET /api/memory/records/sprk_matter/{M} and on POST /api/memory/pins with matterId M, and no pin row appears in Cosmos; a user with AppendTo on M creates a pin;
(b) Compose upload with another user's sessionId returns 404, and check-changes for an item the user cannot see returns 404;
(c) PUT /api/v1/documents/{id} carrying graphDriveId returns 400 and the row's pointer is unchanged (read back);
(d) close-project on a SECURE test project clears only that project's container (permissions read back on another container are unchanged), and on a non-secure test project touches no container;
(e) field-mappings push from the UpdateRelated button on a matter the user can open updates only children the user can write, and a user without Read on the matter gets 404 with no child modifiedon changed;
(f) Office quick-create by a user without the matter Create privilege returns 403 and no row exists;
(g) if the Reporting module is configured in dev, an uncatalogued (workspaceId, reportId) pair returns 404; otherwise record "module not configured; proven by tests only";
(h) POST /api/v1/work-assignments and POST /api/compose/documents/{x}/promote return 404 or 405.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>F0 second door: the read-only check shows that sprk_graphdriveid / sprk_graphitemid are writable by a non-admin Write holder outside the BFF (no fieldpermission rows on them). In that case GET /api/v1/documents/{id}/download and the other app-only row-pointer consumers (DocumentsBulkEndpoints, FileAccessEndpoints, ChatDocumentEndpoints, AppOnlyAnalysisService, DocumentTextSource) still follow a forged pointer. STOP after the PUT fix and present per CLAUDE.md §6: (a) RECOMMENDED: field-level security on the two pointer columns, written only by the BFF, as task 150 did for sprk_issecure (a schema change, so a live gate); (b) server-side pointer verification before every app-only download (the pointer's drive must equal the container RecordContainerResolver derives for the row). Do not ship the PUT fix described as "chain closed".</trigger>
    <trigger>F8: the read-only inventory shows a path that adds external members to a NON-secure project's container, which is the shared business-unit container. (At authoring SpeContainerMembershipService.GrantMembershipAsync has no BFF caller.) STOP: under the server-derived rule, their container permission is never removed at closure, while clearing the shared container would strip every user. Present options; do not clear a ResolvedFallback container.</trigger>
    <trigger>Dead or clientless routes: the zero-caller grep finds a caller for POST /api/v1/work-assignments, POST /api/compose/documents/{documentSpeId}/promote, GET /api/memory/records/… or PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}. A caller counts if it is in src, in the Copilot OpenAPI, in a Power Automate flow named by the owner, or on another project's open branch via /conflict-check. STOP and report the caller. The gated alternative for work-assignments is the G5 shape: CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync for the work-assignment Create privilege, AppendTo on the matter, a team owner via RecordOwnershipResolver, and "Assigned To" for the person, never ownerid = AssignedToUserId. For promote it is the claim tenant, a session owner check and an OBO read of the item, which needs a driveId the body does not carry. For memory records with a sprk_document caller, or PUT with a lookup-setting caller, present the AppendTo / document-filter alternative.</trigger>
    <trigger>F11: an active field-mapping profile's source entity is not in EntityAccessFilter's map, or its target table has no `sprk_regarding{base}` lookup for its source (so the corrected filter cannot be built), or the dev BFF app user cannot impersonate (CannotActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser). STOP and report. Never fall back to an app-only child query or write, and never add a map entry.</trigger>
    <trigger>F14-F16: sprk_report lacks a report-id or workspace column in live metadata, or the stored values are not in the lowercase "D" GUID format, or the Reporting client's reportId turns out to be the catalog row id rather than the Power BI report id. (reportingApi.ts JSDoc says "sprk_report record GUID"; the client sends no workspaceId, so the module returns 400 today.) Also stop if a catalogued report's dataset has no RLS role while holding business-unit-scoped rows: the "businessunit"/"bu" claim never exists, so no token carries a BU role, contrary to docs/guides/reporting-admin.md:384-389. STOP and present: this task's catalog binding assumes the Power BI report id + workspace id contract, and repairing the client contract and the RLS identity is an owner decision.</trigger>
    <trigger>F9/F10 or F12: the live gate shows that a user who legitimately pins facts on a matter they work on lacks AppendTo, or that a user who legitimately quick-creates from Office lacks the Create privilege. STOP and report, rather than widening the rule or reverting to app-only.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any fix appears to need an ADR exception (for example an app-only write with no server invariant, or a new auth service layer under ADR-003): STOP and raise it in the CLAUDE.md §6.5 format.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Every mechanism used already exists and was read for this POML: CallerRecordAccessProbe (GetCallerRightsAsync :212, GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync :342, CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync :386); RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter (:79-233) with EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet (:174); ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter (task 078); QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter; SessionOwnershipFilter, the body-scoped owner check (ComposeActiveDocumentEndpoints.cs:95-124) and ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync (:223); SpeFileStore.GetFileMetadataAsUserAsync (:130-135); RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync (:142); IDataverseUserClient.GetAsync; IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.QueryAsync (over DataverseWebApiService.RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync :1030); UpdateRecordFieldsAsync's impersonateSystemUserId (:1432); TenantResolution.ResolveTenantId; CallerResolution.ResolveObjectId; OperationAccessPolicy "read" / "write" keys. Grep for an existing pin-to-matter operation key: none ("memory.pin" appears only as telemetry counter names in PinnedMemoryEndpoints.cs).</existing>
    <extension>Yes: no new filter class, service, enum or map. Three existing filters gain one optional parameter or one check each (RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter: deny detail; ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter: query-parameter source; QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter: target-table Create privilege). Handlers call existing seams. The one new surface is the OperationAccessPolicy key "memory.pin_matter" = AppendTo: reusing "entity.associate_document" would misdescribe the act (a pin is not a document) and couple two acts that may later need different rights; it carries the three-question justification in the PR. Two routes are deleted, which removes surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this task, any signed-in user can: read any matter's AI record memory (secure matters included); inject text into the AI prompt of every user working on any matter; read another user's uploaded file bytes; run app-only Graph deltas on any container and suppress its change detection; repoint a document row at any SPE item and download it as the managed identity, or file the row under a secure matter without AppendTo; list any container's documents once a one-line type fix lands; strip every user permission from an arbitrary SPE container; mass-write up to 500 children of a matter they cannot see once a one-line bug fix lands; create matters, projects and invoices without the Create privilege; mint embed tokens and run exports for any report the service principal can reach; create user-owned work assignments and app-authored notifications for anyone; and read another user's workspace tabs.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

