  <notes>Owner round 9 (2026-10-03, binding): the sweep's 82 findings are fixed by UAC-r2, one surface task per group; this is the Memory / Compose / remaining group (17). The fix pattern per round 9: reads on the caller's own rights; writes pre-checked as the user, and app-only only for a server invariant; lists trimmed; fail closed with one answer for unknown and denied. Deletions follow the task 083 precedent: dead surface is deleted, not gated, and its waiver goes with it.
Found while authoring or reviewing, recorded for the main session, and NOT silently fixed here:
 • RemoveAllExternalMembersAsync removes every GrantedToV2.User permission, internal users included (SpeContainerMembershipService.cs:296-345), even on a secure project's own container.
 • POST /api/v1/external-access/revoke also takes a client ContainerId (safe only by accident: Guid?).
 • Reporting POST/PUT/DELETE /reports and GET /reports accept any workspaceId, and ReportingEmbedService never uses SP profiles (profileId: null).
 • POST /api/office/todo creates sprk_todo app-only with no Create-privilege check (sweep noteworthy, low; same file as F12).
 • The Compose Save first-save promotion still rebinds (body tenant, body session) with no owner check (sweep noteworthy; deleting the promote route does not touch it).
 • PUT /api/memory/pins/{pinId} answers 404 for an unknown pin and 403 for another user's pin (a pin-existence oracle; pin ids are random).
Folded INTO this task at review: PUT /api/v1/documents/{id} also writes nine parent lookups app-only with no AppendTo (F0 constraint).
Task 167 had not been authored when this POML was written; the main session reconciles its waivers with this task at integration.</notes>

