      <summary>Implements owner round 45 (BINDING, main session under round 15: the f1-v1 verification's answers, and the decision f1-v1 asked for) and closes the verifier's 16 items (note section 22.2). Round 45 item 1: a relocation REPLAYS the source's version history into the copy through the BFF identity, oldest first, the current content last (SpeFileStore.ListFileVersionsAsync, now virtual and following nextLink; ONE new app-only facade method SpeFileStore.DownloadFileVersionAsync); every upload must land on the copy's item with the listed size; any failure deletes the partial copy and leaves the row and the source untouched; the ORIGINAL author, date and size of each replayed version are recorded in the NEW column sprk_document.sprk_relocatedversions (RelocatedVersionHistory) in the same update as the re-point, carried across a second move, reported by GET /api/documents/{id}/versions (VersionInfoDto.LastModifiedBy) and, as dates only, by the external version list; versions-truncated is a stated outcome with counts. Item 2: one copy per in-subtree row, ratified (unchanged). Item 3 / F-B: an unlinked sprk_communicationattachment row is classified by its communication's subtree (RecordContainerResolver.DeriveCommunicationContainersAsync): inside re-keyed to the current file, outside kept, no communication or undecidable pending. Item 4 / F-A: the ledger entry records the source's WITNESS (size, quickXorHash, version) at verification; a repeat call deletes the source by that witness, never by the document's current file (probe Q1 is now a test); a source edited after the move is source-changed-after-move (with the row id) and closed by the relocator's own re-entry: re-copy (the document's file and history plus the source's post-move versions), verify, re-point, settle; every edit is carried, and the last becomes CURRENT only when its author may write the document now (IAccessDataSource, RetrievePrincipalAccess for that person; otherwise history, fail closed). Item 5: F-C tests for V6, V8, V5; F-D the getControl(...).getAttribute().setValue shape, Reflect.set / defineProperty and aliases (import/export rename, re-binding, destructuring) in both detectors, the FLS detector moved to scripts/common/Find-ClientPointerWrite.ps1 and run through pwsh by the new guard test over all 55 cases; F-E gate 23a; the schema script creates both relocation columns field-secured from creation.</summary>
      <decisions>Two decisions made within round 45 and recorded in note 22.12 (no owner question): which content ends current after a re-copy (the last post-move edit only when its author may write the document; reason: the old file stayed writable by the old container's audience); the external version list keeps createdByName null (no author is newly disclosed to external contacts).</decisions>
