    <run date="2026-10-05" branch="task/uac-r2-166-g" base="966f88a21" rigor="FULL" outcome="completed">
      <summary>Implements owner round 54 (BINDING, main session under round 15: the f1-v2 verification's answers) and closes the verifier's 14 items (note section 23.2), classified under owner round 56 (relayed by NOTE-FROM-MAIN.md, read and not committed; this is the lane's last fix round). Round 54 item 1 (class a): the Write check that makes a post-move edit current is read FRESH: DocumentsModule constructs the relocator with the uncached DataverseAccessDataSource, and MayWriteAsync refuses any answer produced before its question (AccessSnapshot.CachedAt &lt; asked), so a Write answer cached by the 60-second CachedAccessDataSource never makes a non-writer's edit current. Item 2 (class a, F-4): the relocation lock is a per-call lease: taken under its own owner id, read back before anything runs (closing IdempotencyService's fail-open acquire and check-then-set race for this caller, #984), renewed every 2 minutes by a heartbeat (10-minute lock), confirmed again before every destructive step (re-point, each ledger entry's settle, source delete, ledger write) and between replay steps; a lost lock stops the move with lock-lost and writes nothing more; release only while still ours. IIdempotencyService gains RenewProcessingLockAsync and an owner-checked ReleaseProcessingLockAsync (default methods; IdempotencyService implements both, the renewal failing closed). Item 3 (class a, F-5): the witness records the time of its content (RelocationWitness.Modified; SpeItemCreator.LastModified from the same uncached item read); post-move versions are ordered by version number, else by time; when the order cannot be decided (five conditions) the result is history-undecidable with the row and the source untouched (retried) - never the current content alone. Item 4 (class b, F-1/F-2/F-3): a biting test for each of Sk, Sq, Si, Sj, Sm, Sw; DocumentVersionListPagingTests drives the real DriveItemOperations.ListFileVersionsAsync through a scripted Kiota adapter, and the listing is bounded (MaxVersionPages 500: throws, never returns a cut history); the KEEP-path header states the witness and lock rules; section 22's seeding claims corrected in place.</summary>
      <decisions>Within round 54 (no owner question): freshness is enforced by the relocator's own rule (testable, ADR-038 B3 bans asserting the DI wiring) as well as by the wiring; in the version-number path "no version above the witnessed one" means the witnessed version was changed in place (its current content is the only content after the witness); a version listing past 500 pages fails the move. Under owner round 56: nothing built for a (d)-(f) item; known limits recorded in note section 23.12.</decisions>
